{
 "title": "The internet ran out of addresses",
 "captions": [
  {
   "text": "The internet ran out of addresses in 2011.",
   "say": "The internet ran out of addresses in twenty eleven.",
   "hide": true
  },
  {
   "text": "Every device online needs an IP address.",
   "say": "Every device online needs an I P address."
  },
  {
   "text": "The original system, IPv4, uses *32 bits.*",
   "say": "The original system, I P version four, uses thirty-two bits."
  },
  {
   "text": "That's about *4.3 billion* addresses.",
   "say": "That's about four point three billion addresses."
  },
  {
   "text": "Sounds like a lot, until there are more phones than people."
  },
  {
   "text": "In 2011, the central pool handed out its !last blocks.!",
   "say": "In twenty eleven, the central pool handed out its last blocks."
  },
  {
   "text": "So your whole home shares one public address."
  },
  {
   "text": "Your router keeps track of who asked for what."
  },
  {
   "text": "The real fix is IPv6, with *128 bits.*",
   "say": "The real fix is I P version six, with a hundred and twenty-eight bits."
  },
  {
   "text": "Enough for every grain of sand on Earth, many times over."
  }
